   "text": {
    "L1": "Land is not shaped the same everywhere. Three main landforms are mountains, plateaus and plains.",
    "L2": "Here is a myth: places higher up are hotter because they are closer to the Sun.",
    "L3": "That belief is wrong. Air gets colder as you go higher, so Shimla is cooler than Delhi.",
    "L4": "Mountains rise steeply and may have peaks, plateaus are raised with fairly flat tops, and plains are low and flat.",
    "L5": "The Himalayas are young and very high, while the Aravallis are among the oldest and worn down.",
    "L6": "Plateaus can provide minerals and black soil for cotton, while rivers build fertile plains with silt.",
    "L7": "Landforms shape life: mountain people use terrace farming and sloping roofs, while plains suit farming, roads and cities.",
    "L8": "So the landform helps explain how people farm, build and travel. Tap the landform that is high and flat-topped."
   },
